# FluentMigrator Migration Patterns

## Project Prefix
- **{ProjectPrefix}** is the identifier of the project (project name or its abbreviation).
- Use a short, consistent prefix per project (e.g. `SM` for Sidae, `PT` for another project).
- In **this project (Sidae)** the prefix is **SM** (or define the one you use in this repo).

## File Naming Convention
- Migration files must use the format: `{yyyyMMdd0000{n}}_{ProjectPrefix}_{TableName}_{Action}_{Object}.cs`
- The file name must match the Migration attribute ID exactly
- **Pattern Components:**
  - `yyyyMMdd0000{n}` - Migration ID (date + sequence number)
  - `{ProjectPrefix}` - Project identifier (see "Project Prefix" above)
  - `TableName` - Name of the table being modified
  - `Action` - One of: `Add`, `Modify`, `Remove`
  - `Object` - One of: `Table`, `Column`, `View`
- **Examples (prefix SM / Sidae):**
  - `20240101000001_SM_Demo_Add_Table.cs` - Adds a new Demo table
  - `20240101000002_SM_Demo_Add_Column.cs` - Adds a column to Demo table
  - `20240101000003_SM_Demo_Modify_Column.cs` - Modifies a column in Demo table
  - `20240101000004_SM_Demo_Remove_Column.cs` - Removes a column from Demo table
  - `20240101000005_SM_Reports_Add_View.cs` - Adds a new view
- The class name should match the file name **excluding the timestamp prefix** (e.g., file `20240101000004_SM_Demo_Add_Column.cs` has class name `SM_Demo_Add_Column`)

## SQL Script Organization
- SQL scripts must be placed in the `Scripts` folder
- SQL script files must use the same base name as the migration file (without .cs extension)
- For migrations that execute SQL scripts:
  - Use `{MigrationId}_{ProjectPrefix}_{TableName}_{Action}_{Object}_Up.sql` for the Up() method
  - Use `{MigrationId}_{ProjectPrefix}_{TableName}_{Action}_{Object}_Down.sql` for the Down() method
- **Examples (prefix SM):**
  - For `20240101000004_SM_Demo_Add_Column.cs`, create:
    - `20240101000004_SM_Demo_Add_Column_Up.sql`
    - `20240101000004_SM_Demo_Add_Column_Down.sql`

## Migration Class Structure
- All migrations must inherit from `Migration` or `BaseMigration`
- Migration attribute must use format: `[Migration(yyyyMMdd0000{n})]`
- Must implement both `Up()` and `Down()` methods
- When using SQL scripts, inherit from `BaseMigration` to use the `ReadScriptFile()` method

## BaseMigration Class
- Use `BaseMigration` as the base class when migrations need to read SQL script files
- The `BaseMigration` class provides a protected `ReadScriptFile(string fileName)` method
- **Example (prefix SM):**
```csharp
[Migration(20240101000004)]
public class SM_Demo_Add_Column : BaseMigration
{
    public override void Up()
    {
        var sql = ReadScriptFile("20240101000004_SM_Demo_Add_Column_Up.sql");
        Execute.Sql(sql);
    }

    public override void Down()
    {
        var sql = ReadScriptFile("20240101000004_SM_Demo_Add_Column_Down.sql");
        Execute.Sql(sql);
    }
}
```

## Naming Pattern Reference
- **Format:** `yyyyMMdd0000{n}_{ProjectPrefix}_TableName_Action_Object`
- **Actions:**
  - `Add` - Creates/adds a new object
  - `Modify` - Alters/changes an existing object
  - `Remove` - Deletes/removes an object
- **Objects:**
  - `Table` - Database table
  - `Column` - Table column
  - `View` - Database view

## Project Configuration
- SQL files in the `Scripts` folder must be copied to output directory
- Add to `.csproj`:
```xml
<ItemGroup>
  <None Include="Scripts\*.sql">
    <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
  </None>
</ItemGroup>
```

